* table_variety -- probes one TABLE with keys of EVERY datatype and reports the census.
* bottleneck: table key handling across every key datatype, not just integers.
* ⭐ WHY THIS EXISTS (hq_P s262, Lon): table_access is integer-keyed only, so the
*   s262 typed-key cure -- one hash function per datatype -- shipped with coverage
*   of exactly ONE of the six types it added.  This kernel exercises integer,
*   string, real and null keys, negative and zero integers, keys that collide,
*   overwrite-in-place, deletion, lookup misses, and a table whose keys are of
*   MIXED type in one table -- the case where "hash by datatype first" is the only
*   thing keeping two different keys apart.
* ⛔ The census is a sum over EVERY probe, so a wrong bucket, a wrong compare or a
*   lost entry changes it.  It is not a smoke test that only proves we ran.
* Standalone:  scrip table_variety.sno   |   sbl -bf table_variety.sno
        &TRIM = 1
        &ANCHOR = 0
        &STLIMIT = -1
        DEFINE('TABLE_VARIETY(N)')                      :(TABLE_VARIETY_END)
TABLE_VARIETY  ZI = 1
        ZS = 0
ZBL     tab = TABLE(64)
*       integers: positive, zero, negative -- all three sign paths of the int hash
        ix = -30
INTFILL tab[ix] = ix * 3
        ix = LT(ix, 30) ix + 1                          :S(INTFILL)
*       strings: short and long, and one that looks like an integer
        sx = 1
STRFILL tab['k' sx] = sx * 5
        tab['a_much_longer_key_' sx] = sx * 7
        sx = LT(sx, 20) sx + 1                          :S(STRFILL)
        tab['17'] = 1700
*       reals, and the null key
        rx = 1
REALFIL tab[rx / 2.0] = rx * 11
        rx = LT(rx, 12) rx + 1                          :S(REALFIL)
        tab[''] = 99
*       ⭐ THE MIXED-TYPE PROBE: 17 and '17' are DIFFERENT keys.  A hash or a
*       compare that ignores the datatype collapses them and the census moves.
        tab[17] = 1717
        ZS = ZS + tab[17] + tab['17']
*       overwrite in place must not add an entry
        tab[5] = 500
        tab[5] = 501
        ZS = ZS + tab[5]
*       read every integer back
        ix = -30
INTREAD ZS = ZS + tab[ix]
        ix = LT(ix, 30) ix + 1                          :S(INTREAD)
*       read every string back
        sx = 1
STRREAD ZS = ZS + tab['k' sx] + tab['a_much_longer_key_' sx]
        sx = LT(sx, 20) sx + 1                          :S(STRREAD)
*       read every real back
        rx = 1
REALRD  ZS = ZS + tab[rx / 2.0]
        rx = LT(rx, 12) rx + 1                          :S(REALRD)
        ZS = ZS + tab['']
*       misses must return the null value, not a neighbour's
        ZS = ZS + SIZE(tab[9999]) + SIZE(tab['absent']) + SIZE(tab[-9999])
        ZI = LT(ZI, N) ZI + 1                           :S(ZBL)
        TABLE_VARIETY = ZS                              :(RETURN)
TABLE_VARIETY_END
*BENCH kernel=TABLE_VARIETY check=40 bud=500 flr=20
        OUTPUT = 'census of one pass  = ' TABLE_VARIETY(1)
        OUTPUT = 'census of 40 passes = ' TABLE_VARIETY(40)
        OUTPUT = 'tab[17] = ' tab[17] '   tab["17"] = ' tab['17'] '   tab[5] = ' tab[5]
END
